# Example age recipient list, for plain age:
#
#   age -R recipients.txt -o secret.age secret.txt
#
# Public keys only, one per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are
# ignored. Nothing here is secret. Each person generates their own keypair
# and sends only the public half, the private key never leaves their machine.
#
# age encrypts the file once with a throwaway key, then stores one copy of
# that key per recipient. Any one private key opens the file on its own.
#
# This file is for age by itself. SOPS does not read it, SOPS takes its
# recipients from .sops.yaml.

